join Dumi (Neutral) left
join Hope (Neutral) right
Dumi: Four pages. It took eleven drafts to get it down to four.
- What does it say?
	Hope: What does it say?
	Dumi: What's shared, who decides, and how somebody joins. That's all it needs to say.
	Dumi: Naledi will chair the water committee. This is the same idea pointed at tools and seed.
Dumi: I studied agricultural economics. Ratios, yields, margins. I was good at it.
- You still are
	Hope: You still are.
	Dumi: I am. And it turns out that's not what I do here.
	Dumi: What I actually do is know who to ask, and remember what people did for each other four years ago, and be careful about whose name goes next to whose.
	Dumi: There's no certificate for that. I've spent about nine years being faintly embarrassed that it's my whole job.
- And now?
	Hope: And now?
	Dumi: Now I've written it into four pages and I'm going to ask the village to vote on it.
	Dumi: Which is the same thing again, isn't it. Knowing who to ask.
Dumi: The gathering stays in the hall. I asked people and they'd already decided — nobody wanted to move it, they were only waiting for someone to say so out loud.
- That someone being you
	Hope: That someone being you.
	Dumi: That someone being me. As usual.
	Dumi: My father used to say the village tells you what you are and you spend twenty years arguing with it.
	Dumi: I've stopped arguing. It's a good hall and I've got the key.
[signal arg="hearts:dumi:2"]
set {GameState.dumi_arc_complete} = true
